file: "packages/core/src/pipeline/delta_render_pipeline.ts"
doc:
  "The diff render pipeline: merge, seed, resolve, restyle by change type, lay out, draw.\n"
  "\n"
  "Vocabulary for this file is fixed in delta_overlay.spec.textproto.\n"
  "\n"
  "This is the pillar's ENTRY POINT and is deliberately called by nothing in\n"
  "this spec. Its caller is renderOp in packages/ops/src/render/op.ts, reached\n"
  "from a new `--delta` flag. That wiring is hand-written and spans two files\n"
  "this pillar does not touch: render_params.ts, for the flag and its zod\n"
  "entry, and op.ts, to load the Delta and to SKIP renderOp's own\n"
  "seedComponentBindings call on this path so that stage 2 here can seed the\n"
  "union diagram instead of the target.\n"
  "\n"
  "It is a sibling of renderPipeline rather than a flag on it. renderPipeline\n"
  "and layoutPipeline both live in render_pipeline.ts and both would have to\n"
  "change to thread an overlay through, which is two modified decls in one\n"
  "existing file -- the shape that has failed convergence every time it has\n"
  "been tried here. The cost is that the layout-then-render tail is written\n"
  "twice; the diff path genuinely has two extra stages between merge and\n"
  "layout, so the two are not the same pipeline with a parameter."

methods: [
  { name: "renderDeltaPipeline"
    doc:
      "Render a target diagram and a Delta together as one SVG string.\n"
      "\n"
      "Six stages, in order:\n"
      "  1. mergeDelta(target, delta) -> the DeltaOverlay.\n"
      "  2. seedComponentBindings(overlay.diagram, stylesheet,\n"
      "     themes.get('default')) -> the stylesheet stages 3 onward use.\n"
      "     When `stylesheet` is undefined, pass a newly created empty\n"
      "     Stylesheet with schemaVersion 1, as renderOp does.\n"
      "  3. resolvePipeline(overlay.diagram, seeded, themes). Note the FIRST\n"
      "     argument: the union diagram from stage 1, never `target`. Passing\n"
      "     `target` would resolve a graph that has no deleted elements in it\n"
      "     and the render would show none of them.\n"
      "  4. applyDiffPalette(resolved, overlay, themes.get('default')?.tokens).\n"
      "  5. layoutEngine.layout, wrapped in a LayoutRequest, exactly as\n"
      "     layoutPipeline does it.\n"
      "  6. SvgRendererImpl().render.\n"
      "\n"
      "`themes` is keyed by BINDING NAME, not by theme name. 'default' is the\n"
      "reserved binding every stylesheet has -- per style.proto's comment on\n"
      "Stylesheet.themes, an unqualified `component` resolves against it --\n"
      "and resolveThemes guarantees an entry for it, falling back to\n"
      "[['default', 'dark']] when a stylesheet binds nothing. So\n"
      "themes.get('default') is a lookup for whichever theme is bound as the\n"
      "default, NOT for a theme literally named \"default\"; a stylesheet\n"
      "binding blueprint to 'default' returns the blueprint theme here.\n"
      "\n"
      "That binding supplies the diff roles because it is the one the canvas\n"
      "background already reads, and a diagram has exactly one background. A\n"
      "stylesheet binding a second theme still styles its own elements from\n"
      "that theme; only the choice between table mode and rotate mode is made\n"
      "once, for the whole picture.\n"
      "\n"
      "Stage 2 is why this function takes the stylesheet renderOp LOADED\n"
      "rather than the one renderOp seeded. Seeding fills in each element's\n"
      "component from the theme's `kind` vocabulary, and it can only do that\n"
      "for elements it can see. renderOp seeds against the target, which by\n"
      "definition contains none of the deleted elements, so a restored node\n"
      "tagged `kind: database` would arrive here with no component and fall\n"
      "back to the theme default -- drawn as a plain rectangle while its\n"
      "surviving neighbours are cylinders. Seeding after the merge is what\n"
      "keeps a deleted element looking like what it was.\n"
      "\n"
      "STAGE 4's POSITION. It must run after stage 3 has RETURNED, because\n"
      "until resolvePipeline's own last stage completes the values it would\n"
      "read are still token reference strings rather than colours. It must\n"
      "run before stage 6, because stage 6 reads the colours. Stage 5 is the\n"
      "only other position available, and running before it rather than after\n"
      "keeps this function's stage order matching the stage names in its\n"
      "error results.\n"
      "\n"
      "Placing stage 4 either side of stage 5 gives the same picture: the\n"
      "diff treatment changes colours, one dash pattern and one fill opacity,\n"
      "never a size, a font metric or a shape, so it cannot change what\n"
      "layout computes. A diff render and a plain render of the same union\n"
      "diagram place every element identically.\n"
      "\n"
      "ERRORS. Stage 3 returns a Result; a failure propagates its\n"
      "PipelineError unchanged, keeping the stage name resolvePipeline gave\n"
      "it. Stage 5 returns Err with stage 'layout' and stage 6 with stage\n"
      "'render', matching layoutPipeline and renderPipeline. Stages 1, 2 and\n"
      "4 have no error channel at all -- each returns its value directly\n"
      "rather than a Result -- so there is nothing to check after them."
    is_async: true
    inputs: [
      { name: "target",       type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.Diagram" } } },
      { name: "stylesheet",   type: { unsupported: { reason: UNION_AT_TYPE_POSITION, source_excerpt: "Stylesheet | undefined" } } },
      { name: "themes",       type: { named: { symbol: "ReadonlyMap", args: [{ primitive: CHARACTER }, { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.theme.v1.Theme" } }] } } },
      { name: "layoutEngine", type: { named: { symbol: "LayoutEngine" } } },
      { name: "delta",        type: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.content.v1.Delta" } } }
    ]
    output: { named: { symbol: "archeglyph.util.Result", args: [
      { primitive: CHARACTER },
      { named: { symbol: "PipelineError" } }
    ]}}
    uses: ["mergeDelta", "seedComponentBindings", "applyDiffPalette", "resolvePipeline", "LayoutRequest", "SvgRendererImpl"]
  }
]
